      "writtenOn": "2015-06-06T01:45:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I notice there are new definitions (*STORAGE_OFF) in chip_config.h of mec1322 drivers. In previous version, CONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF means the address of RW image in flash and we use spi mapping address to access spi data directly. Now, new version uses *STORAGE_OFF to present the offset addresses of RO/RW image in flash and it seems CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF and CONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF both refer to the beginning of CDRAM. So my suggestion is keeping CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF and CONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF 2k alignment and add it in comment to prevent isr table is malfunctional.",
